      "title": "Apple lets Siri AI perform cross-app actions using on-screen context",
      "summary": "Apple announced that developers can integrate Siri AI into all third-party apps in iOS 27.3, released on Tuesday. The update lets Siri complete requests across apps using personal context, natural language prompts, and on-screen awareness.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Available in iOS 27.3 rolling out starting Tuesday.",
        "Developers can integrate Siri AI actions across all third-party apps.",
        "Siri leverages personal context, natural language, and on-screen awareness."
      ],
      "design_implication": "Designing mobile workflows has meant assuming a person navigates every screen and tap target directly. With an OS agent triggering actions through on-screen awareness, interface layouts must expose clear semantic entities and confirmations that an external assistant can safely execute. Audit primary app tasks this week and define explicit confirmation thresholds for actions initiated outside the visible UI.",
